by stof at 2026-02-26T12:15:08Z

@mpdude the deprecation reporting feature of the phpunit-bridge only supports PHPUnit 9 and older. The hacks it uses to hook into the PHPUnit runner are incompatible with the new architecture of the runner in PHPUnit 10+.

We are collaborating with the PHPUnit team to improve the PHPUnit deprecation reporting. I figured out a few weeks ago that the phpunit-bridge classification logic (the logic defining whether a deprecation is self, direct or indirect) has special handling of the DebugClassLoader deprecations, and I now have an in-progress discussion with Sebastian Bergmann to identify the kind of PHPunit extension points that would allow implementing such special logic for the PHPUnit deprecation reporting feature (and potentially also other cases that are currently not well classified even in the phpunit-bridge).

However, classifying the deprecations as direct or indirect is totally separate from deciding whether the deprecation should be triggered or no.

